BLOCKING: none.

ADVISORY a1 (class, pre-existing; W-034 adds one instance): gate-node writers
call doc.setIn(["probationes", <gate>, ...]) without checking the node is a
mapping. A scalar node (`patron: pending`) makes the writer throw an uncaught
"Expected YAML collection at patron. Remaining path: status" (exit 1, stack
trace), not an exit-2 refusal. Nothing is written and no event is emitted, and check
already blocks the input (probatio.shape "gate is not a mapping").
Searched: grep 'setIn(["probationes"' packages/commands/src packages/cli/src (non-test).
Instances: lifecycle.ts:133-136 (ready/spec, by inspection), :379-389 (review,
CONFIRMED by run: same error at "review"), :828-832 (waive, CONFIRMED),
verify.ts:239-241 (by inspection). One fix site would be a shared guard before editOpusFrontMatter. Separate opus.

ADVISORY a2 (single instance): runWaive step 8 is a denylist
(passed/failed/waived refuse) where the brief says "unrecorded, pending or stale" are
admitted. A non-enum status (`patron: { status: bogus }`) is overwritten, exit 0.
All five PROBATIO_STATUSES behave per spec, and check blocks non-enum statuses.
An allowlist is the literal reading. Low severity; fold into a1's opus or W-040.

ADVISORY a3 (single instance, prose drift outside the file list):
branch.ts:222-223's comment still says the removed rule "can no longer trap a
legitimately waived agent/human gate". After W-034 no agent-gate waiver is
legitimate. The comment is stale, not wrong in behaviour.

